  "worked_solution": "We recall the graph of $y={(\\frac{3}{8})}^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013814/assets/99c2329c99005af33f4b62d61547e18dcaa7f04afc931df57439bd1ca08ff35c.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(\\frac{3}{8})}^{x}=\\infty .\n$$",
